; ============================================================
; Tic-Tac-Toe  —  STELLAR terminal game  (loads at $4000, VM1)
; VERSION:  v05  (2026-11-22: v04 + sounds on Q, M; build_tictac_sound.py)
; was:      v04  (2026-07-07) — indexed ops ($2E READIDX / $2F WRITEIDX)
; ============================================================
; Builds on v03. Collapses all 6 board accesses (5 reads + the two
; mark writes) from the ~8-13 byte COPYXA/ADDAI/COPYAX/COPYIMXA
; address-build to a single 4-byte READIDX/WRITEIDX. Also removes the
; R6 address temp (READMOVE's read is now READIDX R4; both writes use
; the index directly). Loop bodies (SCANLINE/PICKEMPTY) run 3 fewer
; opcodes per pass. All 8 CALL targets recomputed for the shift.
;   code 720B (v03) -> 698B (v04).
; Needs firmware v0061.1E (READIDX/WRITEIDX + the 1D zero-extends).
; ============================================================
; ---- SOUND (build_tictac_sound.py) ----
; SOUND (2026-11-22): Q, a speaker or buzzer on it (the web Simulator's Sound button). A click for
; your move and a lower one for the computer's, a buzz for a key that is not 1-9 or a taken cell, and
; a tune at the end (a win, a loss, a draw). M turns the sound off and on ("Sound off" / "Sound on").
; Patches past the program, each reached by a GAL in place of one instruction it then does itself:
;   $4001 GAL PINIT  $4026 GAL PYOU  $406A GAL PCPU  $4096 GAL PWIN  $40A0 GAL PLOSE  $40AA GAL PDRAW
;   $41CC GAL PBAD  $41E4 GAL PTAKEN.  The player (qsound.py, raw 1802, $F1 RUNMC) $4480-$4550;
;   the title and the two notes $4C00; the sound flag $49F8 (1 = on).
; PINIT:
; D 4380 11 05 00 00   LOADXI R5 0000
; D 4384 10 00 01      LOADAI 0001
; D 4387 2F 05 09 F8   WRITEIDX R5 09F8
; D 438B 11 0A 0C 00   LOADXI R10 0C00
; D 438F B0 00 05      GAL 0005
; PYOU:
; D 4392 10 00 01      LOADAI 0001            your mark (as at $4026)
; D 4395 F1 44 80      RUNMC 4480             a click
; D 4398 B0 00 29      GAL 0029
; PCPU:
; D 439B 11 0A 07 42   LOADXI R10 0742        Computer plays (as at $406A)
; D 439F F1 44 89      RUNMC 4489             a lower click
; D 43A2 B0 00 6E      GAL 006E
; PWIN:
; D 43A5 11 0A 07 7E   LOADXI R10 077E
; D 43A9 BD 00 B2      CALL 00B2              *** You win! ***
; D 43AC F1 44 9B      RUNMC 449B             a rising tune
; D 43AF 00            HALT                   the end (as before)
; PLOSE:
; D 43B0 11 0A 07 93   LOADXI R10 0793
; D 43B4 BD 00 B2      CALL 00B2              *** Computer wins! ***
; D 43B7 F1 44 A4      RUNMC 44A4             a sad tune
; D 43BA 00            HALT                   the end (as before)
; PDRAW:
; D 43BB 11 0A 07 AE   LOADXI R10 07AE
; D 43BF BD 00 B2      CALL 00B2              *** Draw! ***
; D 43C2 F1 44 AD      RUNMC 44AD             two plain notes
; D 43C5 00            HALT                   the end (as before)
; PBAD:
; D 43C6 86 09 00 6D   TESTXI R9 006D
; D 43CA A0 03 DE      IFTRUEI PMUTE
; D 43CD 86 09 00 4D   TESTXI R9 004D
; D 43D1 A0 03 DE      IFTRUEI PMUTE
; D 43D4 11 0A 07 52   LOADXI R10 0752        Enter 1-9! (as at $41CC)
; D 43D8 F1 44 92      RUNMC 4492             a buzz
; D 43DB B0 01 D0      GAL 01D0
; PMUTE:
; D 43DE 11 05 00 00   LOADXI R5 0000
; D 43E2 2E 05 09 F8   READIDX R5 09F8
; D 43E6 81 00 00      TESTAI 0000
; D 43E9 A0 03 FA      IFTRUEI PMON
; D 43EC 10 00 00      LOADAI 0000
; D 43EF 2F 05 09 F8   WRITEIDX R5 09F8
; D 43F3 11 0A 0C 4E   LOADXI R10 0C4E
; D 43F7 B0 01 D0      GAL 01D0               print it, ask again
; PMON:
; D 43FA 10 00 01      LOADAI 0001
; D 43FD 2F 05 09 F8   WRITEIDX R5 09F8
; D 4401 F1 44 B6      RUNMC 44B6             a beep: it is on
; D 4404 11 0A 0C 5A   LOADXI R10 0C5A
; D 4408 B0 01 D0      GAL 01D0
; PTAKEN:
; D 440B 11 0A 07 5F   LOADXI R10 075F        Cell taken! (as at $41E4)
; D 440F F1 44 92      RUNMC 4492             a buzz
; D 4412 B0 01 E8      GAL 01E8
; ---- END OF SOUND ----

